## Context
Second audit pass after the wave-1 raid surfaced 13 small code-quality
and transparency items. Many are minor; the meaningful refactors are
the duplicated header-line predicates and the migrate.go layout block
extraction.

## Code health (8 items)
1. **Unused `jsonEscape`**: defined in `erg.go:373` but ready.go uses
   `encoding/json` instead. Delete.
2. **`parseErg` one-line wrapper inlineable**: after PR #126 introduced
   `parseErgBytes`, `parseErg` is just `ReadFile` + delegate. Only 2
   call sites left (loadErgs at line 353, cmdValidate at validate.go:325).
   Either inline both call sites and drop `parseErg`, OR document why
   the wrapper stays (callers that want default-file-read ergonomics).
   *Note: 0117 will reshape this surface; consider deferring.*
3. **`printReadyText` redundant param**: receives both `totalCount` and
   `openEntries`; `totalCount == len(tickets)` at the only call site.
   Collapse — `src/go/ready.go:111`.
4. **`removeBlockedByRef` re-walks ticketDir**: close.go:120 walks the
   dir non-recursively while `loadErgs` already exists. Unify via a
   shared loader to keep one parse-path and one filter rule.
5. **Triple-duplication of header-key-prefix predicates**:
   `isClosedHeaderLine` (erg.go:332), `isStatusHeaderLine` (migrate.go:288),
   `isTagsHeaderLine` (migrate.go:300) duplicate the same "line starts
   with key" pattern. Fold into `hasHeaderKey(line, key string)` helper.
6. **Exported names in ergspecv1.go**: `MagicLine`, `IsoDateRE`,
   `FilenameRE`, `LogLineRE`, `ValidTagValues` are exported despite
   single-package use. Unexport now that the post-0116 schema is stable.
7. **`migrate.go` layout-upgrade block is ~85 lines** inside
   `cmdMigrate` (lines 102-185). Extract to `migrateLayout(dir)` for
   readability and testability.
8. **`Line` type alias re-litigation**: previous audit flagged it as
   pure documentation; design decision was to keep. Recorded; NOT
   changing.

## Code transparency (5 items)
9. **`helpClose` says "three-step atomic operation"** but step 3
   iterates many files non-atomically. Misleading — `src/go/close.go:17`.
10. **`summary<Cmd>` consts lack doc comments** explaining the
    "printed by printUsage via the commands registry" contract — all
    12 command files.
11. **`migrate.go:54` generic message**: "directory not found" prints
    for any `os.Stat` error (permission, broken symlink, etc.).
    Distinguish or use `fmt.Errorf("...: %w", err)`.
12. **`manualPreamble` empty-build-stamp behavior undocumented**: if
    `buildDate`/`vcsRevision` are empty, the line becomes
    `"Generated from: erg"` — the const doc doesn't mention this.
    `src/go/main.go:27-46`.
13. **`parseErgBytes` doc missing HasLogSep edge case**: the comment
    doesn't warn that body-quoted `--- log ---` / `--- body ---`
    literals set `diag.HasLogSep`/`HasBodySep` to true even though
    they're not actual separators — `src/go/erg.go:193-196`.

## Out of scope
- Defer-to-0117: item 2 (parseErg wrapper) if 0117 lands first will
  rewrite the entire parser signature; drop item 2 in that case.
- Defer-to-0118: nothing here.

## Exit criteria
- All 13 items addressed (or items 2 explicitly deferred to 0117).
- `make test` passes.
- No exported-name churn breaks tests (item 6 is package-internal so
  should be safe — verify).
